1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,578
Sixty-five million American homes have a thermostat that can adjust itself.

2
00:00:04,698 --> 00:00:06,183
Guess how many actually let it.

3
00:00:06,303 --> 00:00:13,449
According to the government's household energy survey, about fifty-two and a half million homes have a programmable thermostat,

4
00:00:13,569 --> 00:00:15,884
and almost thirteen million have a smart one.

5
00:00:16,004 --> 00:00:20,386
But only about twenty million say it adjusts the temperature automatically.

6
00:00:20,506 --> 00:00:21,676
About three in ten.

7
00:00:21,796 --> 00:00:25,159
Fifty-one million just set one temperature and leave it there.

8
00:00:25,279 --> 00:00:26,523
That's where the savings are.

9
00:00:26,643 --> 00:00:32,602
ENERGY STAR certified smart thermostats have to cut heating run time by at least eight percent,

10
00:00:32,722 --> 00:00:34,145
and cooling by at least ten.

11
00:00:34,265 --> 00:00:38,940
For a home with gas heat and central air, that's roughly a hundred dollars a year.

12
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:41,236
So check that your schedule is on tonight.

13
00:00:41,356 --> 00:00:43,867
Sixty-five million homes could be doing this.
